# AquariusOS — nothing updates AND restarts the computer by itself (2026-10-21).
#
# Fedora's bootc base switches on bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
# (86-bootc-standard.preset). That timer runs `bootc upgrade --apply`, which
# downloads a new system AND REBOOTS THE MACHINE WITHOUT ASKING — in the middle
# of an export, if that is when it fires. On AquariusOS updates come from GNOME
# Software instead: it downloads in the background and then shows "Restart to
# update", and you choose when.
#
# Presets are read lowest number first and the first match wins, so this "10-"
# beats Fedora's "86-". Step 77 also MASKS the timer, which is what reaches
# machines that were installed before this file existed.
# Guide: docs/restart/updater.md
disable bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
disable bootc-fetch-apply-updates.service
